From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: Recover tray icons when their XEmbed host disappears.

An embedded icon can lose its X window when the tray host is destroyed.
DestroyNotify clears whole_window and asks explorer to hide/show the icon.
When the replacement tray uses the same visual, set_window_visual does
not recreate the window; SystrayDockInsert can therefore send a dock
request with XID zero and report success. Recreate a missing X window
before marking it embedded and sending the request.

There is a separate accounting problem when the icon temporarily falls
back to explorer's standalone tray. The X11 driver retains its embedded
flag. Calling SystrayDockRemove on that fallback icon can then return
TRUE and set icon->display to HIDDEN before systray_remove_icon sees it.
The standalone tray's displayed count is never decremented and its empty
window stays visible even after the external tray returns.

Only call the driver's dock-removal path for ICON_DISPLAY_DOCKED icons,
leaving standalone icons to the existing systray_remove_icon path.

These are generic XEmbed recovery fixes relevant to GNOME tray-manager
recreation during lock/unlock. They do not change SNI selection or menu
focus handling, and require runtime confirmation on the affected GNOME
session.

Related: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/803#issuecomment-5896271090
---

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -3443,6 +3443,14 @@
 
     if (!(data = get_win_data( hwnd ))) return FALSE;
     set_window_visual( data, &visual, TRUE );
+    /* The tray host may have destroyed the embedded X window. An unchanged
+     * visual does not recreate it, but a new dock request needs a valid XID. */
+    if (!data->whole_window) create_whole_window( data );
+    if (!data->whole_window)
+    {
+        release_win_data( data );
+        return FALSE;
+    }
     make_window_embedded( data );
     window = data->whole_window;
     release_win_data( data );

diff --git a/programs/explorer/systray.c b/programs/explorer/systray.c
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -671,8 +671,11 @@
 
     if (icon->display == ICON_DISPLAY_HIDDEN) return;  /* already hidden */
 
-    if (enable_dock && NtUserMessageCall( icon->window, WINE_SYSTRAY_DOCK_REMOVE, 0, 0,
-                                          NULL, NtUserSystemTrayCall, FALSE ))
+    /* A formerly docked icon can now belong to our fallback tray. In that
+     * case systray_remove_icon must remove it from the displayed icon count. */
+    if (icon->display == ICON_DISPLAY_DOCKED && enable_dock &&
+        NtUserMessageCall( icon->window, WINE_SYSTRAY_DOCK_REMOVE, 0, 0,
+                           NULL, NtUserSystemTrayCall, FALSE ))
     {
         icon->display = ICON_DISPLAY_HIDDEN;
         icon->layered = FALSE;
